WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:03.060
- [Narrator] The US election
is taking up airtime

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.500
on Russian state television

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.653
as the ballots are still being counted.

00:00:07.526 --> 00:00:11.443
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:19.928 --> 00:00:20.940
(crowd cheering)

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.350
- [Narrator] Four days after election day,

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.640
the Associated Press
and other media outlets

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.830
declared former vice president
Joe Biden the winner.

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:30.910
He had garnered the 270
Electoral votes needed

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:34.130
to defeat President Trump in
the race for the White House.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.840
But Russia's main television networks

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.840
are taking extra effort to cast out

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.805
on Biden's victory in
the eyes of its viewers.

00:00:40.805 --> 00:00:44.170
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.160
- [Narrator] Russian state networks

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.200
are using the elections as an opportunity

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.290
to portray American democracy as messy.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:54.207
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.298
- State media occupies an enormous role

00:00:59.298 --> 00:01:00.960
in the Russian media landscape.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.820
In terms of informing people
and informing opinions,

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:07.030
it really does play a very large role.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:08.120
- [Narrator] There are three main themes

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.600
shaping Russian public opinion

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.160
about US politics,

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.120
such as election irregularities,

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.180
the question about who calls the winner

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:18.221
and the stark preview of
the new administration.

00:01:18.221 --> 00:01:21.920
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.430
- [Narrator] There's no
apparent coordination

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.090
between Russian state media
and the Trump campaign

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:28.510
but Russian media have
echoed a familiar line

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:29.590
from the Trump campaign

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:31.620
about election irregularities.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.280
- It's amazing how those mail-in ballots

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.795
are so one sided.

00:01:34.795 --> 00:01:38.712
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.947
- [Narrator] There's been no
evidence of widespread fraud

00:01:46.947 --> 00:01:49.350
but the Trump campaign
has turned to the courts,

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:52.363
challenging absentee and
mail-in voting procedures.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.170
While the news casts
appear to support Trump

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.280
and not Biden,

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.452
it's ultimately signaling
something else to viewers.

00:02:00.452 --> 00:02:01.920
- I think that a big part of this

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.260
is not really to come down
on one side or the other

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:07.520
but to rather sow doubt in people's minds

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.510
about the electoral process,

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.330
about the nature of democracy itself

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.837
in the United States.

00:02:12.837 --> 00:02:16.650
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.310
- [Narrator] Russian
anchors also have questions

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:21.033
about who's calling the results in the US.

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:24.950
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.100
- [Narrator] For over a century,

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:29.140
US presidential elections have been called

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.300
by news organizations

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.810
before the official results are announced.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:35.090
That's because it can take
weeks to certify the results

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:38.850
since each state has different
rules and regulations.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.130
- NBC News now projects that Joe.

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:41.960
- [Narrator] News
organizations based their calls

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:43.320
on near-complete vote counts

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.040
by election officials in each state.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:49.040
Plus the US doesn't have a
national elections commission

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.550
to announce the winner.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:53.520
But in Russia, there's a
Central Election Commission

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.810
and so to Russian viewers,

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.910
the American way of calling
the election is unusual.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.060
- Who was it called by?

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:00.913
All of them.

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:01.950
Oh my goodness.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.373
All the networks.

00:03:03.373 --> 00:03:05.485
Wow.

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:07.280
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:08.340
- [Narrator] Biden's critical comments

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:09.440
about Russia over the years.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.830
- Get out of Ukraine.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.520
- [Narrator] Are repeated across
different political shows.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.560
He's portrayed as someone
who will not be nice

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.520
or at least neutral to Russia.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.070
Biden frequently criticized
Russia's foreign policy

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.330
and strongly supported sanctioning Moscow

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:26.035
for annexing Ukraine's
Crimean Peninsula in 2014.

00:03:26.035 --> 00:03:29.952
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:32.972 --> 00:03:34.840
(dramatic music)

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:36.480
- [Narrator] The focus isn't just on Biden

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.570
but also people possibly being considered

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.684
to join his administration.

00:03:40.684 --> 00:03:44.601
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.340
- That certainly does get across the idea

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:50.824
that Joe Biden is not the
favorite candidate of the Kremlin,

00:03:50.824 --> 00:03:53.400
given some of the things that
Biden has said about Russia.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.180
- I think the biggest
threat to America right now

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:59.510
in terms of breaking up our security

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.916
and our alliance is Russia.

00:04:01.916 --> 00:04:03.690
But Biden has also indicated a willingness

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.620
to work with the Kremlin on the extension

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:07.130
of an arms control treaty,

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:10.208
something that Moscow has
also shown interest in.

00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:14.125
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.500
- [Narrator] Nearly three
out of four Russians

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.150
get their new from television

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.520
and so the message that
state media broadcasts send

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:23.134
about the future administration reaches

00:04:23.134 --> 00:04:25.797
large audiences across Russia.

00:04:25.797 --> 00:04:29.714
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.492
- [Narrator] Beyond who
sits in the White House,

00:04:32.492 --> 00:04:34.810
Russia's rolling coverage of the election

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:37.675
has a deeper message
about American democracy.

00:04:37.675 --> 00:04:40.740
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:41.700
- [Narrator] But with its constantly

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:43.430
changing political landscape,

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.320
it isn't one to be envied.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:46.520
- The more time passes,

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:50.047
the more you see differences
between the US political system

00:04:50.047 --> 00:04:51.500
and the Russian political system,

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.990
which in name calls itself a democracy.

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:55.730
Things stay very much the same in Russia

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.930
and I think the idea that they're trying

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:58.763
to get across here

00:04:58.763 --> 00:05:03.763
is that you have this
kind of vibrant democracy

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:06.640
but it's flawed at its roots

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.710
and so that in the end kind

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:11.040
of leaves the Russian
people with no alternative

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.160
to imagine a Russian political system

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.510
that could be anything else

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:16.863
beyond Vladimir Putin staying in power.

